t=fact(t,4,r'''[F4] Measurable direct integrals and factor representations use [[def-direct-integral-of-unitary-representations]] and [[def-factor-representation-and-primary-representation]]. Separable representations have central factor decompositions, which for type-I groups refine over the actual dual with canonical measure class and multiplicity ([[thm-central-decomposition-into-factor-representations]], [[thm-irreducible-direct-integral-decomposition-for-type-i-groups]], [[thm-essential-uniqueness-of-type-i-irreducible-disintegration]]). The existence proof's ideal-support argument will be displayed for the present Hilbert–Schmidt field, rather than inferring its intrinsic diagonal algebra from labels alone.''')
